1
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:05,672
(Penny:)Hey, Leonard, check this out.

2
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:12,223
(Sheldon:)Leonard, she's doing it again.

3
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:15,844
(Leonard:)I think it upsets Sheldon
when you play with the food.

4
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:20,016
(Sheldon:)No, it upsets Sheldon when she
willy-nilly takes it from the containers...

5
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:22,976
(Sheldon:)...without regard
for its equitable distribution.

6
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:26,188
(Sheldon:)This is essentially
why you have famine in India.

7
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,951
(Penny:)You want me to put it back?

8
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,575
(Bernadette:)-Leonard?
-It upsets Sheldon...

9
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:36,032
(Leonard:)...when you play with the Sheldon.

10
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,956
(Howard(arriving):)What's up, my nerdizzles?

11
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:44,256
(Howard(arriving):)Raj, Sheldon, I want you
to meet my girlfriend, Bernadette.

12
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:45,799
(Sheldon:)-Hello.
-Leonard, Penny.

13
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:48,382
(Howard:)-You know my girlfriend, Bernadette.
-Yeah. Hey.

14
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:51,178
(Howard(arriving):)Bernadette,
say "fo'shizzle" to my nerdizzles.

15
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,800
(Bernadette:)I don't think I can.

16
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:56,849
(Bernadette:)I don't have Howard's street cred.

17
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:01,813
I hope it's all right, I told Bernadette
she could join us for dinner.

18
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:04,978
(Leonard:)-Sure. The more, the merrier.
-No, that's a false equivalency.

19
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,528
(Sheldon:)More does not equal merry.

20
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:09,821
(Sheldon:)If there were 2000 people in this apartment,
would we be celebrating?

21
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,566
(Sheldon:)No, we'd be suffocating.

22
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,318
(Leonard:)-Sheldon.
-Don't "Sheldon" me.

23
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:15,990
(Sheldon:)-We ordered for five people, not six.
-It's fine.

24
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,239
We'll put it on the table, family-style.

25
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:21,121
Oh, sure. Why don't we put our hands
behind our backs...

26
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,669
(Sheldon:)...have an old-fashioned
eating contest?

27
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:27,500
(Leonard:)Relax. It'll be fine. Sit down, you guys.

28
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,380
ALL EXCEPT BERNADETTE: No.
-What?

29
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,300
(Penny:)Oh, yeah, you can't sit there.

30
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:36,759
(Bernadette:)-Why not?
-That's where Sheldon sits.

31
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,260
(Bernadette:)He can't sit somewhere else?

32
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:42,806
In the winter, that seat's close enough
to the radiator...

33
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:45,267
...so he's warm
yet not so close that he sweats.

34
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:47,728
(Penny:)In the summer,
it's in the path of a breeze...

35
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:49,779
(Penny:)...created by opening windows there.

36
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:53,363
(Penny:)It faces the television at an angle
that isn't direct so he can talk...

37
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,820
(Penny:)...yet not so wide
that the picture looks distorted.

38
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:05,020
(Sheldon:)Perhaps there's hope for you after all.

